      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Only three runners in a race decimated by scratchings. ANOTHER CHAMPERS (3) returned in good order with a close-up second at Ipswich before not measuring up in town last time out. Is one from one over this course and distance and is sure to find this assignment much easier. Rates the testing material against this line-up. LA PREMIERE (2) shed the maiden tag at Kilcoy when resuming and will have derived a stack of confidence from that win. Gets 3kg weight relief with the claim and can go right on with the job now. BARBARIAN KING (4) resumes here but showed enough in his first campaign to warrant consideration in a race like this.",
